# Exclude test fixtures and golden corpora so `matlatl check .` over its own
# repo analyzes only the real, human-curated docs (README, docs/, ADRs). The
# fixtures under testdata/ are deliberately broken/orphaned inputs for the test
# suite and would otherwise drown out genuine doc-link rot.
testdata/
**/testdata/
internal/infrastructure/emit/testdata/

# The offline evaluation harness has private gold, generated fixtures, and
# task-package instructions that must not enter this repository's dogfood graph.
eval/

# The demo corpus (demo/corpus/) is a deliberately broken/orphaned sample used
# to show off matlatl's findings on stage; exclude the whole demo/ tree so the
# repo's own strict doc-gate sees only the real docs.
demo/

# Claude Code agent scaffolding. `.claude/agent-memory` (and peers) hold
# agent-generated notes that use an internal `[[slug]]` linking convention which
# does not resolve to repo documents, so they only produce phantom broken-link /
# unreachable findings. ADR 0010 deliberately leaves these to per-repo config
# rather than a tool-wide default-ignore — this is that per-repo opt-out.
.claude/

# CLAUDE.md is a symlink to AGENTS.md (single source of truth, so Claude Code
# picks up the same agent guide). matlatl doesn't follow symlinks (ADR 0003);
# ignoring it keeps the repo's own dogfood run notice-clean.
CLAUDE.md

# Generated output directory.
out/
